/**
 * A single ground control point: one real-world location whose position is
 * known in BOTH latitude/longitude and floor plan pixel coordinates.
 *
 * Plain value type, embedded in {@link GeoCalibration#points}; it has no
 * identity and is not independently persistable.
 *
 * Each point is one constraint in the least-squares fit described on
 * {@link GeoCalibration}. The two coordinate pairs must describe the *same*
 * physical spot — a mismatch of a few meters between the lat/lon and the pixel
 * reading is the single most common cause of a transform that is subtly and
 * confusingly wrong across the whole floor.
 */
type CalibrationPoint {

  /**
   * Human-readable note identifying the physical feature this point marks,
   * e.g. "NW outside corner of building" or "center of rotunda".
   *
   * Purely for maintainability — whoever re-calibrates later needs to find the
   * same spot. Not used in the fit.
   */
  label: string

  /**
   * Latitude of the control point in decimal degrees (WGS84).
   */
  lat: !double

  /**
   * Longitude of the control point in decimal degrees (WGS84).
   */
  lon: !double

  /**
   * X coordinate of the same physical point on the floor plan image, in pixels
   * from the image's left edge.
   *
   * Must fall within 0 to {@link Floor#imageWidth} of the owning floor.
   */
  imageX: !double

  /**
   * Y coordinate of the same physical point on the floor plan image, in pixels
   * from the image's TOP edge (+Y points down).
   *
   * Must fall within 0 to {@link Floor#imageHeight} of the owning floor.
   */
  imageY: !double
}
